<title>HONG KONG: Shanghai Ind announces 1st final results.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Ind announces 1st final results.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>				     Proforma Combined</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   75.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    12.9</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  17.64 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    360.42</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,200.63</p>
<p>    Company name		 Shanghai Industrial Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>				     Consolidated</p>
<p>				     January 9 to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   72.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    12.9</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  17.64 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    247.03</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,317.41</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 5-8</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 22</p>
<p>NOTE - Shanghai Industrial manufactures pharmaceuticals, personal care products, tobacco and packaging materials.</p>
<p>The company was incorporated in Hong Kong on January 9, 1996, and listed on the Stock Exchange on May 30.</p>
<p>The company had reported in its interim results an exceptional gain of HK$17.64 million on subscription monies received on flotation of the company.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
